WEBVTT

00:00:00.100 --> 00:00:03.705
Operating near structures increases collision, turbulence, navigation, signal,

00:00:03.705 --> 00:00:05.056
and visual-occlusion risk.

00:00:05.056 --> 00:00:10.013
Maintain safe standoff, simple escape paths, visual awareness, and conservative speed.

00:00:10.013 --> 00:00:15.420
Do not enter spaces or fly beneath structures without specific authorization, capability,

00:00:15.420 --> 00:00:16.321
and procedures.

00:00:16.321 --> 00:00:23.080
Power lines and energized equipment can be difficult to see and may create serious electrical,

00:00:23.080 --> 00:00:24.882
electromagnetic, or operational hazards.

00:00:24.882 --> 00:00:29.388
Coordinate with the asset owner and use their required boundaries.

00:00:29.388 --> 00:00:32.993
A zoom lens is safer than unnecessary proximity.

00:00:32.993 --> 00:00:38.400
Control exposure to people and vehicles through scheduling, barriers, observers, site escorts,

00:00:38.400 --> 00:00:39.751
and route design.

00:00:39.751 --> 00:00:45.158
Stop when unbriefed activity enters the operating area or the crew can

00:00:45.158 --> 00:00:47.411
no longer maintain required separation.

00:00:47.411 --> 00:00:52.368
Sensitive sites may restrict imagery, radio use, mapping, cloud processing, storage,

00:00:52.368 --> 00:00:53.269
or disclosure.

00:00:53.269 --> 00:00:55.071
Confirm requirements before arrival.

00:00:55.071 --> 00:00:59.126
Protect credentials, firmware, controllers, networks, media, and inspection systems.

00:00:59.126 --> 00:01:01.379
Collect only scoped asset evidence.

00:01:01.379 --> 00:01:04.984
Avoid unrelated homes, people, security features, or operations.

00:01:04.984 --> 00:01:09.039
Limit access and retention, and document purpose and authorization.

00:01:09.039 --> 00:01:11.743
Inspection is not permission for surveillance.

00:01:11.743 --> 00:01:15.798
Abort criteria include weather deterioration, signal or navigation uncertainty,

00:01:15.798 --> 00:01:21.205
aircraft warnings, obstacle conflict, people or vehicles entering the area, privacy concerns,

00:01:21.205 --> 00:01:23.908
lost communication, or poor data quality.

00:01:23.908 --> 00:01:27.063
Safe recovery takes priority over completing coverage.

00:01:27.063 --> 00:01:31.568
At critical sites, coordinate radio use, cybersecurity, photography restrictions, escorts,

00:01:31.568 --> 00:01:35.173
emergency procedures, and data transfer with the owner.

00:01:35.173 --> 00:01:40.580
Do not assume an aviation approval overrides industrial, security, or process-safety controls.
